[h1]Taoist — v6.3.3[/h1]
A [b]hardcore rework[/b] of the base game: a living world, a harsh economy, towns you can rule, families, lifelong storylines, tougher battles, new paths of cultivation, houses of your own, cultivator clans, and now [b]7 special constitutions[/b].
Most features can be tuned or turned off in [b]S&M Configs[/b] (title screen). The harder your settings, the higher your S&M score and the better your rewards. If it gets too hard, combine it with other mods.
Give me a like to let me know it is useful, thanks! If you want to support the work: [url=https://ko-fi.com/fouru]Ko-fi[/url]
News, questions and bug reports: join the [url=https://discord.gg/XKaP3EYfw]Discord server[/url]!

[h2]⚠ Requirements[/h2]
[list]
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3385996759]Fouru's ModLib[/url] v2.3.08 or newer
[*][b]Move ModLib to the TOP of your mod list[/b], then [b]restart the game[/b].
[/list]

[h2]★ New in 6.3[/h2]
[b]Seven constitutions[/b]
[list]
[*][b]Pill Body, Sword Bone, Vajra Body, Innate Spirit Body, Dragon Blood Body, Thunder Body, Venom Body[/b]: special bodies of 10 tiers each, every tier a destiny with its own name
[*]They awaken from what you do (potions, battles with an art, treasures, herbs, lightning...): a rare chance at first, then they grow with their points. Your realm caps the tier. Some are born with one, and NPCs awaken them too
[/list]
[b]Potions that keep up[/b]
[list]
[*]The Pill Body and your alchemy rank raise the recovery of your potions in battle
[*]Rare encounter (realm 8+): the [b]Nine-Turn Golden Pill[/b], after which every potion also heals 10% of your max HP / MP
[*]New storyline [b]The Medicine King's Testament[/b] (from Golden Core): an old alchemist, three missing pages, and a lasting gift for your potions
[/list]
[b]Windows and balance[/b]
[list]
[*]New windows: your constitutions, the 6 artisan arts and their ranks, trainee and merchant ranks, rebirth (conditions, gains, costs)
[*]Monsters grow slower by grade, special monster shields follow their max HP, MP blocks cost by the damage blocked
[*]New S&M page "Skills & pills": mastery exp, MP cost, cooldown, power-up pills...
[/list]
[b]Also[/b]: the title screen shows the other mods of the author, and a Support button (Ko-fi); the Body Refining window no longer overlaps its texts; the S&M bank fee goes up to +1,000% (was +10,000%).

[h2]Features in short[/h2]
[b]New game[/b]: starting divine artifacts, destinies of your choice, skip the intro, roles for the player and NPCs (Power, Speed, Tao, Atk, Def, Angel, Evil, Merchant), S&M presets (Level 0-10), one-life mode, in-game trainer.

[b]S&M score[/b]: every setting is worth points; the score changes battle exp and loot (-20% to +50%), gives a title and a start bonus, and is recorded for every character.

[b]Storylines[/b]: 17 NPC storylines (19 with Dao of Creation) with portraits, real battles, several acts, time limits and endings (Cold Sword, Hundred-Year Wager, Roadside Inn, Heart Demon...). Failed acts open another path, and the lines remember each other.

[b]World and NPCs[/b]: NPCs grow, craft, earn titles, take dao companions and have children. Hire a team, NPCs join your battles, stalkers chase rare items, random encounters, reworked dramas, quests and commissions.

[b]Families and legacy[/b]: household upkeep, family accounts, family tree; when you die, play on as your child or grandchild.

[b]Economy[/b]: inflation and currency reform, bank accounts and storage fees, bank loans with debt collectors, a player market with NPCs (negotiation, barter, buy orders), sect contribution exchange.

[b]Towns[/b]: budgets, taxes, town masters and guardians, bounties and wanted hunters, your own house, cultivator clans with their elders, feuds and clan wars.

[b]Cultivation[/b]: five more paths (Body Refining, Merit & Karma, Artisan Dao with 6 crafts and ranks, Dao Heart, Spirit Sense), 7 constitutions, long seclusions while the world keeps living, Qi cultivation, spirit stone cultivation, natural breakthroughs, rebirth, time skips.

[b]Battle[/b]: mana shields, special and growing monsters, reworked damage with block / evade / crit, the [b]Damage Calc[/b] window (F9), losses on defeat, refining of rings, outfits, artifacts and mounts, several divine artifacts with hotkeys.

[b]Interface[/b]: Taoist Settings, the Taoist log (month by month), icons in texts, optional hidden battle map / previews / damage multiplier / Damage Calc button.

[b]Languages[/b]: English, Chinese (Simplified and Traditional), Korean, Japanese, Vietnamese, Thai, Russian, German, French, Spanish, Latin, plus a custom language system.

